>I finally have a character with rings of polymorph and polymorph
>control at the same time.  Suddenly I realized that I had no idea
>on how to go about polymorphing myself!  Here's a few questions
>that I hope you nethackers of the world could answer:
> 
>* Exactly how do you polymorph yourself?   Didn't find a command
>  (like teleport's ^T), do you have to zap yourself with a wand
>  of polymorph, or am I missing something obvious (never delved
>  into self-polymorphing until now).
With a ring of polymorph, polymorphing occurs randomly. If you wait long
enough, it will happen.
> 
>* Which monsters are best to polymorph into?
Vampire Lords. You get an extra bite attack that can level drain your
opponents. You can wear all your armor. Your armor class goes down by
about 10. Vampire Lords have the curious ability to levitate and still
be able to pick up stuff. You can cross water this way, but if you change back
to human form, you go for a swim. Another good one is a Marilith, but
you break out of your armor and cloak, so take them off first. You get
5 attacks with your weapon as one of these. Few monsters can take 5 hits
from Frosty and sitll live...
> 
>* How do you avoid having all your armor torn to shreds, do you
>  simply take it off, polymorph, then see what fits?
Don't polymorph into anything large. Vampire Lords are human size, but
Mariliths, Xorn, and Rust Monsters are larger. These are the only
other monsters that, IMO, you need to poly into.
> 
